laurel 2600: Bluetooth on the Mi A3. WCN3990 over the GENI UART of QUP1 SE9 (0x4c90000, GPIO 10-13 qup14): GCC wrap 1 votes + s4 RCG (DFS levels or the Linux table), FIFO mode, polled, RTS/CTS. Power: PM6125 L9/L16/L17/L23 through the RPM (topaz_rpm_write), power pulses 0xC0 at 2400 and 0xFC at 115200 (no BT_EN). Bring-up as Linux hci_qca/btqca: EDL version (vendor event), 0xfc48 to 3000000 baud, crbtfw%02x.tlv rampatch + crnv%02x.bin NVM (speed tag 17) read at run time from the phone's FAT16 bluetooth_b (then _a) partition, HCI reset, BD_ADDR (the chip's own if unique, else the ADT local-mac-address, 0xfc14 + read back). iOS side (negroni 0332/0333/0336/0337 path): kernel control com.apple.uart.bluetooth, /dev/uart.bluetooth, /dev/cu.bluetooth, /dev/btwake, HCI answers for bluetoothd's Broadcom vendor commands, in-band sleep bytes. LaurelBluetooth.cpp: ADT /arm-io/bluetooth nub gets the address in use, or is hidden when Bluetooth is off. One line: 'LAUREL BT: on: WCN3990 product .. rom .., crbtfw21.tlv + crnv21.bin, 3000000 baud, BD_ADDR ..' or 'LAUREL BT: off: <why>'. Kill switch laurelbt=0. One small file per step (bsd/dev/laurel_bt*.c). Details: docs/laurel_sprout/bluetooth.md.

